== DESIGN (one mechanism, no second lane model) ==
- godot/scripts/lane_bands.gd (NEW, 77 lines): paint_lane_bands(m) iterates
  m.lanes, skips every non-"ground" kind, and mounts ONE MeshInstance3D per
  ground lane named LaneBand_<id>: mesh = one quad per waypoint segment
  (corners at wp ± halfwidth along the segment normal, y BAND_Y 0.02 > 0,
  upward-facing tris; degenerate segment draws nothing instead of a NaN
  normal); material = ONE shape built in code (unshaded + TRANSPARENCY_ALPHA
  + pinned BAND_COLOR = the lit-translucent read). Zero writes on m beyond
  add_child; m.map_def NEVER read (the band rides build_lanes' public records).
- mission_world.gd (+7 lines, file stays <=250): const preload + ONE
  LANE_BANDS.paint_lane_bands(m) call in build_cores beside the G1 hook +
  header/one comment block. mission.gd ZERO lines (at the 400 ceiling).
- Kit godot/sim/g2_lane_band_probe.gd (g1 boot idiom verbatim; rows
  LB-BANDS n=3 ground=3 (count == ground-lane count) / LB-BAND per-lane node
  at origin + one-quad-per-segment vertex count + pinned material literals /
  LB-WPS every ground wp is the EPS(0.05)-midpoint of a vertex pair spread by
  BAND_WIDTH — the band walks the SAME polyline the sim walks / LB-NEG air=2
  banded=0 — negative leg, an inverted kind filter cannot survive it).
  HARDENED beyond G1 this session: a GDScript runtime error aborts a function
  SILENTLY — first real run proved it (rc stayed 0, LB-OK still printed over
  a stderr script error) — so LB-OK now prints only on the pass's own
  completion flag, and the test pins LB-OK as the LAST transcript row plus
